rota lap 4319, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in. Its threshold asks what already stands
rota true before anyone argues with it, and its dual seat is `the marked value`: every value that
rota crosses a seam wears a mark naming its type, and an absorb-express pair is earned by a real
rota crossing rather than built on speculation. That is exactly what this lap did. One reading was
rota carrying two kinds of trailing whitespace; the mark that tells them apart is the `\\` at the
rota head of the line, read at the door before any argument about tidiness, which is the fixed
rota seat's two-rooms habit one layer down. The cardinal seat's test -- could this number turn
rota out to be wrong? -- named the other finding: 17 could, and was.

think Took the second of the three TAME hand lists named on the card, `tame_check`, following my
think own last lap's recommend. `tame_check_scan.rish` held 16 paths inline; the roster,
think `TAME_CORE.md` and my own log all said 17.
think Measured the population before touching anything. The twenty rooms in
think `tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_rooms.txt` hold 1,127 authored `.rye`. Unlike the opening triad
think this scan reads EVERY authored file rather than the hosted subset, because a tab and a
think trailing space are faults whichever way a file opens -- so the two widened guards read two
think different populations off one roster, on purpose, and each says which.
think Four readings over the 1,127: qualified assert 0, `Self = @This()` 0, tab 0, trailing
think whitespace 3. I widened each predicate past the elder literal while I was there --
think `std[.]debug[.]assert[[:blank:]]*[(]` and `Self[[:blank:]]*=[[:blank:]]*@This[(][)]` --
think and all three still read zero, so the widening reaches further and costs nothing.
think Then I read the three trailing-whitespace files rather than sweeping them, which is the
think whole of this lap's finding.
think `glow/lower_named_cast.rye:468,662` and `brushstroke/brush_parse.rye:793` carry the space
think inside a `\\` multiline string literal. Those bytes are generated Zig and generated Brush --
think what the program EMITS. Stripping them changes output, not tidiness.
think `brushstroke/font8x8_data.rye:35` is the glyph row for the space character, and its `//`
think comment IS a space. Ninety-four neighbors name their glyph; strip this one and the row
think reads as an unnamed blank.
think So the reading split in two rather than gating at 3 or exempting by path. `trailing_content`
think is reported and gated nowhere, on the line the ASCII comment guards already drew: program
think content is not the subject. `trailing_authored` is a ratchet at 1, which a day that names
think the glyph in words lowers honestly -- where a named exemption would hide it forever.

obs THE 17 WAS NEVER A FILE COUNT EITHER. The elder witness printed `length lines result.out`
obs and said "all 17 files"; the list held 16 and the seventeenth was the trailing empty line --
obs the same fault as yesterday's 25-for-24, in the guard standing beside it, found the same day.
obs Two of two widened guards had been measuring their own output. I checked the third rather
obs than assuming: `rune_assert_sweep` counts 12 real arguments handed to its scan, so the class
obs fired exactly twice and `grep -rn 'length lines' tools/ --include=*.rish` now returns one
obs assertion in a bounds selftest and this repair's own comment. Not booked: both instances are
obs repaired in this commit and the third is proven clean, which is an account rather than an
obs allocation.
obs SHELL_DIALECT CAUGHT MY FIRST DRAFT, AND IT WAS RIGHT TO. I reached for `grep -P` twice --
obs once for `\t` and once for a negative lookahead splitting the trailing-whitespace reading.
obs The guard gates PCRE at zero. The lookahead was never needed: `grep -H` lists every
obs trailing-blank line and a second `grep -v` drops the ones opening a `\\` string. The tab
obs reading went to `awk`, whose ERE spells a tab as `\t` inside single quotes, so neither a tab
obs byte nor a nested double quote had to enter the file. My second attempt at the tab read
obs `grep -lF \"$T\"`, and Rishi passes `\"` through as a literal quote character rather than as
obs shell quoting -- so `$T` word-split away and the reading came back 1126 of 1127. A wall that
obs would have shipped as a wall at zero, reading everything.
obs MY SHELF LINK KEPT THE CARD'S DEPTH. Shelving the elder GRASS account carried
obs `](archive/20260908-125347_...)` down one directory, where it should read
obs `](20260908-125347_...)`. `fold_shelf_link` named it with the single correction attached.
obs NOT MINE, NAMED RATHER THAN TAKEN: `crushed_index` reds on `press/date has no row on
obs docs-geode/press/README.md`, landed today in `1f023a30a`. `docs-geode` is petrichor's lane
obs and `press/` is a closed stack, so my own seat says name a find rather than take it.
obs `standing_equipment` reds because it reports that one plus `dated_path` (%626, Keaton's).

